(i) Farey-neighbor identity: 1/n & 2/(2n-1) adjacent in F_{2n-1} (cross-product +-1):
   n= 3: 1/3 , 2/5: cross-product = -1 (|.|=1 => Farey neighbors: True)
   n= 4: 1/4 , 2/7: cross-product = -1 (|.|=1 => Farey neighbors: True)
   n= 5: 1/5 , 2/9: cross-product = -1 (|.|=1 => Farey neighbors: True)
   n= 6: 1/6 , 2/11: cross-product = -1 (|.|=1 => Farey neighbors: True)
   n= 7: 1/7 , 2/13: cross-product = -1 (|.|=1 => Farey neighbors: True)
   n= 8: 1/8 , 2/15: cross-product = -1 (|.|=1 => Farey neighbors: True)
   n= 9: 1/9 , 2/17: cross-product = -1 (|.|=1 => Farey neighbors: True)
   n=10: 1/10 , 2/19: cross-product = -1 (|.|=1 => Farey neighbors: True)
   n=11: 1/11 , 2/21: cross-product = -1 (|.|=1 => Farey neighbors: True)
   n=12: 1/12 , 2/23: cross-product = -1 (|.|=1 => Farey neighbors: True)
